{
  "_doc": "Outfit base (docs/OUTFIT-BASE.md). Every look is the base, then a style (archetype), then the equipped armour item, then the boots item, merged in that order (src/core/outfit-look.js resolveOutfit). palette: hex colours or \"$tunic\" (the character's chosen tunic colour). cut: how the base garments are cut and painted (src/render/garments.js): sleeve/cuff are 0..1 from shoulder to wrist (sleeve > 1 is full length, a shorter sleeve shows the arm), hem is metres below the hips where the top ends (max 0.16 = the base hoodie), trim is the piping width at hems and openings (m), panel the half width of the front placket (m), yoke the depth of a two-tone shoulder yoke below the neck (m, 0 = none), stripe the half width of a stripe along the top of each sleeve (m), neck the depth of a V neck (m, 0 = closed), pants 0..1 from hips to ankle where the trousers end, boot 0..1 from hips to ankle where the boot shaft starts (painted in the shoes colours), pattern 0 none / 1 hem bands / 2 dots on the main colour, tails the coat-tail length below the hips (m). parts: raised pieces from src/render/outfit.js PARTS; an item's `drop` removes base/style parts.",
